2. PRODUCT SCOPE
2.1 In-Scope Features
Phase 1: Core Functionality (MVP - Months 1-8)

✅ Historical crime data ingestion and preprocessing
✅ DBSCAN/HDBSCAN clustering for hotspot identification
✅ LSTM-based temporal risk forecasting
✅ Dynamic risk scoring algorithm (DCTI)
✅ Mobile application (iOS/Android) with basic alerts
✅ Interactive heatmap visualization
✅ User registration and authentication
✅ Basic route safety scoring

Phase 2: Enhanced Features (Months 9-12)

✅ Women Safety Mode with isolation detection
✅ Safe route navigation with multiple path options
✅ Crowdsourced incident reporting
✅ Authority dashboard with analytics
✅ Push notification system
✅ Offline map caching
✅ Emergency contact integration
✅ Alert threshold configuration (authority feature)

Phase 3: Advanced Capabilities (Months 13-18)

✅ Edge AI deployment for low-latency predictions
✅ Explainable AI outputs for authorities
✅ Advanced patrol optimization algorithms
✅ Trend forecasting and emerging hotspot detection
✅ Multi-city deployment architecture
✅ API for third-party integrations
✅ Incident management dashboard

2.2 Out-of-Scope Features
The following features are explicitly excluded from current product development:
Excluded from All Phases:

❌ IoT sensor network integration (gunshot detection, crowd sensors, smart lighting)

Rationale: Requires third-party hardware partnerships and municipal infrastructure not available in most cities
Future consideration: Phase 4 (Year 2+) when smart city infrastructure matures


❌ CCTV/Computer vision analysis

Rationale: Privacy concerns, regulatory complexity, high computational costs
Future consideration: Phase 5 with strict privacy frameworks


❌ Facial recognition or person identification

Rationale: Violates ethical AI principles and EU AI Act
Future consideration: Never (fundamentally incompatible with product values)


❌ Individual person risk scoring or predictive profiling

Rationale: Illegal in EU, unethical, high bias risk
Future consideration: Never


❌ Direct 911/emergency dispatch integration

Rationale: Regulatory approvals required, liability concerns
Future consideration: Phase 4 with proper legal frameworks


❌ Private property monitoring

Rationale: Privacy violations, requires explicit property owner consent
Future consideration: Phase 4 with opt-in frameworks


❌ Wearable device biometric monitoring

Rationale: Health data privacy regulations (HIPAA-like), limited hardware partnerships
Future consideration: Phase 3-4 with major wearable manufacturers


❌ Social media sentiment analysis

Rationale: High false positive rate, privacy concerns, API limitations
Future consideration: Phase 4 with validated methodologies


❌ Blockchain-based data verification

Rationale: Technology not mature enough, high cost, limited value-add
Future consideration: Reassess in 2027+

2.4 Data Sources
Primary Data Sources (Required for MVP)

Official Crime Records

Police department FIR databases
Government open data portals (data.gov, police APIs)
Emergency service call records (anonymized)
Minimum 3 years historical data required


Crowdsourced Reports

User-submitted incident reports via mobile app
Community safety feedback
Women-specific safety markers


Environmental Data

Weather conditions (visibility, precipitation)
Public event calendars
Transit schedules
Business operating hours



Secondary Data Sources (Optional Enhancements)

Census demographic data
Street lighting databases
Point-of-interest (POI) data
Traffic flow data

Excluded Data Sources (Current Phase)

Real-time IoT sensor feeds
CCTV video streams
Social media posts
Cellular location tracking

2.5 Technology Constraints
Must Use:

Location-based risk assessment only (no person profiling)
Open-source ML libraries where possible
Cloud-agnostic architecture
Standard REST APIs
Industry-standard encryption

Must Avoid:

Proprietary ML models requiring licensing
Platform-locked technologies
Privacy-invasive tracking methods
Unauditable "black box" AI


4. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
4.1 Data Management Module
FR-DM-001: Crime Data Ingestion
Priority: P0 (Critical)
User Story: As a system administrator, I want to automatically ingest crime data from multiple sources so the system has up-to-date information.
Description: System shall automatically ingest historical crime data from government open data APIs and uploaded CSV files.
Acceptance Criteria:

Support API integration for real-time data feeds (REST APIs)
Accept manual CSV/Excel file uploads via web interface
Parse minimum required fields: crime_type, latitude, longitude, occurred_at
Validate data quality:

Flag missing required fields
Reject invalid coordinates (lat: -90 to 90, lon: -180 to 180)
Flag future dates as errors
Detect duplicate records (same location + time + type within 100m / 1 hour)


Log all ingestion errors with detailed error messages and timestamps
Process minimum 100,000 records within 5 minutes
Support incremental updates (delta loads, not full refresh)
Maintain data lineage (source, ingestion timestamp)

