Alert content: Type, location, time (no personal details)
Respects user privacy (anonymous by default)



Abuse Prevention:

User reputation score (based on verified reports)
Automatic suspension after 3 false reports
Manual review for suspicious patterns

5. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
5.1 Performance Requirements
NFR-P-001: Response Time
Description: System shall respond to user interactions within acceptable latency thresholds to ensure smooth user experience.
Acceptance Criteria:

API Response Time:

p95 < 200ms (95th percentile)
p99 < 500ms (99th percentile)
p99.9 < 1000ms


Mobile App:

Startup time (cold start): < 3 seconds
Startup time (warm start): < 1 second
Heatmap loading time: < 2 seconds
Route calculation time: < 5 seconds
Screen navigation: < 300ms


Dashboard:

Page load time: < 3 seconds
Chart rendering: < 500ms per chart
Data query response: < 1 second



Measurement Method:

Application Performance Monitoring (APM) tools (New Relic, Datadog)
Synthetic monitoring (Pingdom, UptimeRobot)
Real User Monitoring (RUM)


NFR-P-002: Throughput
Description: System shall handle expected user load and data volume without performance degradation.
Acceptance Criteria:

Concurrent Users:

Support 100,000 concurrent active users
Sustained load: 50,000 users
Peak load: 150,000 users (during events)


API Requests:

Handle 1,000 requests per second (sustained)
Peak: 2,500 requests per second


Location Updates:

Process 10,000 location updates per second
Each update triggers geofence check


Push Notifications:

Send 50,000 push notifications per minute
Batch processing for efficiency



Load Testing:

Use Apache JMeter or Locust
Simulate realistic user behavior patterns
Test scenarios:

Normal load (50K users)
Peak load (150K users)
Spike test (sudden 3x increase)
Endurance test (sustained load for 24 hours)




NFR-P-003: Scalability
Description: System architecture shall support horizontal scaling to accommodate user growth.
Acceptance Criteria:

Horizontal Scaling:

API servers: Auto-scale from 2 to 20 instances
ML inference servers: Auto-scale from 1 to 10 instances
Database: Read replicas (up to 5)


Auto-Scaling Triggers:

CPU utilization > 70%
Memory utilization > 80%
Request queue depth > 100


Scaling Speed:

New instance provisioned within 2 minutes
Instance added to load balancer within 30 seconds


Database:

Vertical scaling: Up to 64 vCPUs, 256GB RAM
Sharding strategy defined for >10M crime records



Architecture:

Stateless API servers (no session affinity required)
Sticky sessions disabled (use JWT tokens)
Shared cache layer (Redis cluster)
CDN for static assets (CloudFlare, CloudFront)


5.2 Reliability Requirements
NFR-R-001: Availability
Description: System shall maintain high availability to ensure users can access safety features when needed.
Acceptance Criteria:

System Uptime: 99.9% (monthly)

Allowed downtime: < 45 minutes per month
< 720 minutes per year


Planned Maintenance:

Weekly maintenance windows: Off-peak hours (2-4 AM local time)
Advance notice: 7 days for planned downtime


Deployment Strategy:

Zero-downtime deployments using blue-green strategy
Rollback capability within 5 minutes



Monitoring:

Uptime monitoring (Pingdom, UptimeRobot)
Alert on downtime within 1 minute
Incident response SLA: 15 minutes acknowledgment


NFR-R-002: Fault Tolerance
Description: System shall continue operating gracefully in presence of component failures.
Acceptance Criteria:

Database Failover:

Automatic failover to replica within 30 seconds
Primary-replica architecture with synchronous replication
Replica lag < 1 second


External API Failures:

Retry logic: 3 attempts with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s)
Circuit breaker pattern: Trip after 5 consecutive failures
Fallback behavior defined for each API


ML Service Failures:

Serve cached predictions if ML service down
Cache TTL: 1 hour
Degrade gracefully: Use historical average if cache miss


Message Queue:

Dead letter queue for failed messages
Retry failed messages up to 5 times
Alert on persistent failures




NFR-R-003: Data Integrity
Description: System shall ensure data accuracy and consistency across all operations.
Acceptance Criteria:

Database Transactions:

ACID compliance for critical operations (user registration, incident reporting)
Use database transactions for multi-table updates


Foreign Key Constraints:

Enforce referential integrity
Cascade deletes where appropriate
Prevent orphaned records


Data Validation:

Validation at API layer (input sanitization)
Validation at database layer (constraints, triggers)
Validation at application layer (business logic)


Audit Trails:

Log all data modifications:

Who (user_id)
What (action)
When (timestamp)
Previous value, New value


Immutable audit logs (append-only)




5.3 Security Requirements
NFR-S-001: Authentication & Authorization
Description: System shall implement robust authentication and authorization mechanisms to protect user data and system resources.
Acceptance Criteria:

Authentication:

JWT tokens with 24-hour expiration
Refresh tokens with 30-day expiration
Token rotation on refresh
Secure token storage: iOS Keychain, Android Keystore


Password Security:

Hashing: bcrypt with cost factor 12
Salt: Unique per user (handled by bcrypt)
Minimum password strength enforced


Account Security:

Account lockout: 5 failed attempts in 15 minutes
Lockout duration: 15 minutes
Email notification on suspicious login (new device, new location)


HTTPS/TLS:

All communications over HTTPS (TLS 1.3)
Certificate pinning in mobile apps (prevent MITM)
HSTS headers (HTTP Strict Transport Security)



Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):

Enforce permissions at API level
Verify user role on every request
Principle of least privilege


NFR-S-002: Data Protection
Description: System shall protect sensitive user data through encryption and privacy controls.
Acceptance Criteria:

Encryption at Rest:

Database: AES-256 encryption
File storage: Server-side encryption (S3 SSE)
PII fields encrypted at column level


Encryption in Transit:

TLS 1.3 for all API communications
Certificate pinning in mobile apps


Data Anonymization:

Location data aggregated for analytics (no individual tracking beyond 24 hours)
User IDs hashed in analytics databases
IP addresses masked in logs (last octet: 192.168.1.xxx)


GDPR Compliance:

User can export their data (JSON format)
User can delete their account and data
Data retention policies enforced:

Location history: 7/30/90 days (user configurable)
Deleted accounts: Grace period 30 days


Consent management for data collection


Sensitive Fields Masking:

Passwords never logged
Email addresses partially masked in logs (u***@example.com)
Phone numbers masked (555-***-1234)




NFR-S-003: API Security
Description: System shall protect APIs from abuse and malicious attacks.
Acceptance Criteria:

Rate Limiting:

100 requests per minute per user (authenticated)
20 requests per minute per IP (unauthenticated)
HTTP 429 response when limit exceeded
Retry-After header included


Input Validation:

Whitelist allowed characters (alphanumeric + specific symbols)
Maximum field lengths enforced
Type checking (string, number, boolean)
SQL injection prevention: Parameterized queries only
XSS prevention: Output encoding


CORS Policies:

Restrict API access to authorized origins
Whitelist: Web dashboard domain, mobile app domains
Credentials allowed only for whitelisted origins


API Keys (for third-party integrations, Phase 3):

Unique keys per integration
Key rotation every 90 days
Revocation capability


SQL Parameterization:

Never concatenate SQL strings
Use ORM (SQLAlchemy, Django ORM) or prepared statements




5.4 Usability Requirements
NFR-U-001: User Interface
Description: User interfaces shall be intuitive, accessible, and easy to navigate.
Acceptance Criteria:

Navigation Efficiency:

Any feature accessible within < 3 taps/clicks
Clear information architecture
Breadcrumb navigation in dashboard


Accessibility Compliance:

WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance
Screen reader support (VoiceOver, TalkBack)
Keyboard navigation (web dashboard)
Minimum tap target size: 44x44 pixels (iOS), 48x48dp (Android)
Color contrast ratio: 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI elements


Color-Blind Friendly:

Use patterns in addition to colors
Risk levels indicated by icons + colors
Tested with color-blindness simulators


Font Sizes:

Adjustable font sizes: Small, Medium (default), Large
Respect system-wide text size settings
Minimum font size: 12pt




NFR-U-002: Localization
Description: System shall support internationalization for future expansion.
Acceptance Criteria:

Phase 1 (MVP):

English language support only
Framework in place for future languages (i18n)


Phase 2-3:

Spanish, French, Hindi support
Translation files externalized (JSON, gettext)


Locale-Specific Formatting:

Date/time display in user's local timezone
Distance units:

Metric (km): Default for non-US users
Imperial (miles): US users


Currency: Based on deployment region
Number formatting: Respect locale (1,000 vs 1.000)




NFR-U-003: Onboarding
Description: New users shall be guided through app features efficiently.
Acceptance Criteria:

First-Time User Tutorial:

Skippable (don't force users)
Highlight key features: Heatmap, Alerts, Women Safety Mode
Max 5 screens


Contextual Help Tooltips:

Display on first use of complex features
"?" icon for help text
Link to detailed help articles


Demo Mode:

Allow users to explore without real location
Sample data for testing
Clear indication: "Demo Mode - Sample Data"


In-App FAQ:

Searchable help articles
Categories: Getting Started, Features, Privacy, Troubleshooting




5.5 Compatibility Requirements
NFR-C-001: Mobile Platforms
Description: Mobile apps shall support wide range of devices and OS versions.
Acceptance Criteria:

iOS:

Minimum version: iOS 13.0 (covers 95% of devices as of 2026)
Tested on: iPhone 8, iPhone SE (2020), iPhone 12, iPhone 15
iPad support: Responsive layout for larger screens


Android:

Minimum version: Android 8.0 (API level 26) (covers 90% of devices)
Tested on: Samsung Galaxy S10, Google Pixel 5, OnePlus 9
Tablet support: Responsive layout


Screen Sizes:

Small phones: 4.7" (iPhone SE)
Standard phones: 6.1" (iPhone 12)
Large phones: 6.7" (iPhone 15 Pro Max)
Tablets: 7"-12"


Responsive Layout:

Adapts to screen size
No horizontal scrolling
Readable text on all sizes




NFR-C-002: Web Browsers (Dashboard)
Description: Authority dashboard shall work across modern web browsers.
Acceptance Criteria:

Supported Browsers:

Chrome 90+ (primary)
Firefox 88+
Safari 14+
Edge 90+


Unsupported: Internet Explorer (end of life)
Responsive Design:

Desktop: 1920x1080 (primary), 1366x768
Tablet: 1024x768 (iPad landscape)
Mobile: 375x667 (iPhone fallback, but desktop version recommended)


Feature Detection:

Graceful degradation if browser lacks features
Polyfills for older browsers (within supported versions)




NFR-C-003: Network Conditions
Description: Apps shall function acceptably on various network conditions.
Acceptance Criteria:

Minimum Connection:

Functional on 3G networks (minimum 1 Mbps)
Optimized for 4G/5G
WiFi support


**Offline Mode**:

Cached maps valid for 24 hours
Cached risk data valid for 1 hour
Queued actions: Reports, alerts sync when online
Progressive Loading:

Load critical content first
Lazy load images
Show loading indicators


Bandwidth Optimization:

Compress API responses (gzip)
Optimize images (WebP, progressive JPEG)
Minimize API calls (batching, caching)




5.6 Compliance Requirements
NFR-CO-001: Privacy Regulations
Description: System shall comply with applicable data privacy regulations.
Acceptance Criteria:

GDPR Compliance (EU users):

User consent for data collection
Right to access: Users can export data
Right to erasure: Users can delete account + data
Right to portability: Data export in machine-readable format (JSON)
Data retention: Configurable retention periods
Privacy policy clearly explaining data usage


CCPA Compliance (California users):

Disclosure of data collected and purposes
Right to opt-out of data selling (we don't sell, but must disclose)
Right to delete personal information


Privacy Policy:

Clear, non-legalese language
Updated date displayed
Version history maintained
Consent required before account creation


Data Retention Policies:

Crime records: 5 years
User data: Active + 1 year post-deletion (30-day grace)
Location history: User configurable (7/30/90 days)
Logs: 90 days


