10. TESTING STRATEGY
10.1 Unit Testing
Scope: Individual functions and components
Tools:

Backend: pytest, unittest (Python)
Frontend: Jest, React Testing Library

Coverage Target: Minimum 80% code coverage
Key Test Cases:

Data preprocessing functions (cleaning, validation)
Risk score calculation algorithm (DCTI)
Authentication and authorization logic
API input validation
Geofencing point-in-polygon calculations
Route pathfinding algorithm
Alert threshold configuration logic


10.2 Integration Testing
Scope: Component interactions and API endpoints
Tools: Postman, pytest with test database
Test Scenarios:

End-to-end user registration and login flow
Risk score API returning correct data from ML service
Route calculation integrating risk scores correctly
Push notification delivery to mobile devices
Database CRUD operations with proper constraints
ML model retraining pipeline
Alert triggering based on geofencing


10.3 Performance Testing
Scope: System performance under load
Tools: Apache JMeter, Locust
Test Scenarios:

API latency under increasing concurrent users (100, 1000, 10000)
Database query performance with millions of crime records
ML inference latency for batch predictions
Push notification delivery at scale (10,000+ simultaneous)
Heatmap rendering performance
Route calculation with large datasets

Acceptance Criteria:

API p95 latency < 200ms
Support 10,000 concurrent users
Risk score calculation < 50ms
Zero errors under sustained load


10.4 Security Testing
Scope: Vulnerability assessment and penetration testing
Tools: OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite
Test Areas:

SQL injection attempts
Cross-site scripting (XSS) vectors
Authentication bypass attempts
Authorization privilege escalation
API rate limiting effectiveness
Password strength enforcement
Token expiration and refresh
HTTPS/TLS configuration
Data encryption at rest and in transit


10.5 User Acceptance Testing (UAT)
Scope: Real-world usage by pilot users
Participants: 50-100 beta testers (citizens and police officers)
Duration: 4-6 weeks
Feedback Collection:

In-app surveys (NPS, CSAT)
User interviews (qualitative feedback)
Analytics on feature usage (Google Analytics, Mixpanel)
Bug reports and feature requests (Jira, GitHub Issues)

Success Criteria:

80%+ user satisfaction rating (CSAT ≥ 4/5)
<5% crash rate
Average session duration >5 minutes
70%+ users return within 7 days (7-day retention)


11. DEPLOYMENT PLAN
11.1 Deployment Architecture
Cloud Provider: AWS / Google Cloud / Azure (cloud-agnostic design)
Infrastructure as Code: Terraform
Container Orchestration: Kubernetes (EKS/GKE/AKS)
CI/CD Pipeline: GitHub Actions

11.2 Environments
Development Environment

Purpose: Active development and initial testing
Data: Synthetic/anonymized sample data
Access: Development team only
Deployment: On every commit to dev branch
Infrastructure: Single instance, minimal resources

Staging Environment

Purpose: Pre-production testing and QA
Data: Anonymized production-like data (full dataset)
Access: Development, QA, Product teams
Deployment: On merge to staging branch
Infrastructure: Mirrors production (scaled down 50%)

Production Environment

Purpose: Live system serving real users
Data: Real production data
Access: Operations team, restricted developer access (read-only)
Deployment: Manual trigger after staging approval
Infrastructure: Auto-scaling, multi-availability zone


11.3 Deployment Process
1. Code Commit (Developer pushes to GitHub)
   ↓
2. Automated Tests (Unit + Integration)
   ↓ (Pass)
3. Build Docker Images (Multi-stage build)
   ↓
4. Push to Container Registry (Docker Hub, ECR)
   ↓
5. Deploy to Development (Automatic)
   ↓
6. Manual QA Sign-off (Product team approval)
   ↓
7. Deploy to Staging (Automatic)
   ↓
8. Automated Smoke Tests (Critical paths)
   ↓
9. UAT and Performance Testing (Load tests)
   ↓
10. Product Owner Approval (Final go/no-go)
   ↓
11. Blue-Green Deployment to Production
    - Deploy new version (Green environment)
    - Run health checks (API endpoints, database connectivity)
    - Switch traffic from Blue to Green (DNS/Load Balancer)
    - Monitor for 1 hour (error rates, latency, user feedback)
    - Rollback if errors detected (switch back to Blue)
   ↓
12. Post-Deployment Monitoring (24-hour watch)
Blue-Green Deployment Details:

Blue: Current production version
Green: New version being deployed
Traffic Switch: Load balancer routing change (instant)
Rollback: Switch traffic back to Blue (<5 minutes)


11.4 Rollback Strategy
Automated Rollback Triggers:

Error rate > 5%
API latency p99 > 1000ms
Database connection failures
Critical service unavailable

Manual Rollback:

Product owner decision
Critical bug discovered post-deployment
Execution time: < 5 minutes

Rollback Procedure:

Switch load balancer back to Blue environment
Verify Blue environment health
Investigate Green environment issues
Keep Green running for debugging
Deploy fix to Green, repeat deployment process


12. MAINTENANCE & SUPPORT
12.1 Model Retraining Schedule
ModelFrequencyTrigger ConditionsDowntimeDBSCAN ClusteringMonthly (1st of month, 2:00 AM)New crime data > 5% of training setNone (cached predictions serve during retraining)LSTM ForecastingWeekly (Sunday, 2:00 AM)Prediction accuracy < 75%NoneRisk Score CalibrationBi-weeklyFalse positive rate > 15%None
Retraining Process:

Background job (no user impact)
New model validated before deployment
A/B testing for significant changes
Rollback capability


12.2 Monitoring & Alerts
Metrics to Monitor:

Performance:

API response times (p50, p95, p99)
Database query performance
Model prediction latency


Reliability:

Error rates by endpoint
Service uptime
Database connection pool usage


Business:

User session duration and retention
Alert false positive/negative rates
Push notification delivery success rate
Daily/monthly active users



Alerting Thresholds:

Critical: Error rate > 5%, API downtime, database unavailable

Notification: PagerDuty (SMS + Phone call)
Response SLA: 15 minutes


Warning: Latency spike (p99 > 800ms), high memory usage (>85%), low disk space (<20%)

Notification: Slack, Email
Response SLA: 1 hour



On-Call Rotation:

24/7 support with escalation procedures
Primary on-call engineer (1-week rotation)
Secondary on-call for escalation
Incident commander for critical outages


